    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Two ways to write it, and they do exactly the same thing. Store each step in a variable if you want the reading order to be obvious — sidebar, then the region, then the switch. Or run the whole thing together as one chain. I use the variables when I'm debugging, honestly, because I can print each one and see what it found.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "test_settings.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "what it searches",
          "color": "purple",
          "atWord": 2.333,
          "caption": "same locator, two spellings",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "sidebar = page.get_by_role(\"complem…\")",
              "detail": "search the whole page for this",
              "sub": "one sidebar found",
              "label": "step 1",
              "atWord": 9.917
            },
            {
              "text": "notif = sidebar.get_by_role(\"region\","
            },
            {
              "text": "    name=\"Notifications\")",
              "detail": "now search only INSIDE it",
              "sub": "the rest of the page is gone",
              "label": "step 2",
              "atWord": 16.75
            },
            {
              "text": "notif.get_by_role(\"switch\","
            },
            {
              "text": "    name=\"Email alerts\").click()",
              "detail": "and only inside that",
              "sub": "one switch, no ambiguity",
              "label": "step 3",
              "atWord": 23.667
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "# or all in one go:"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_role(\"complementary\") \\",
              "detail": "the same thing, chained",
              "sub": "pick whichever reads better",
              "label": "chained",
              "atWord": 34.583
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 539,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-17-advanced-locators_long_s06.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "BROWSER_STEP",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "And on the page? It's this ordinary. Into the sidebar. Then the Notifications block inside it. Then the toggle, and it flips. Nothing clever happening anywhere, no explicit waiting, and not one nth-child in sight. So if a designer reorders those blocks tomorrow morning, this test doesn't care even slightly — the directions still hold, because the sidebar is still the sidebar.",
      "data": {
        "browserStep": {
