      "durationFrames": 616,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-17-advanced-locators_long_s15.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "And this is the punchline. The code for reaching inside a shadow root is just… the code. There's no shadow locator function, no piercing flag, no special anything. You write the line you'd have written if the shadow DOM had never existed, and it works. Which is the whole point — the complexity is somebody else's problem now.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "test_shadow.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "the result",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.667,
          "caption": "the boring code IS the feature",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "# <fancy-datepicker> hides its input"
            },
            {
              "text": "# inside a shadow root."
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "# Selenium: execute_script, tears, etc."
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "# Playwright: just locate it, as normal:",
              "detail": "no piercing flag exists",
              "sub": "because none is needed",
              "label": "nothing",
              "atWord": 11.667
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_label(\"Departure date\") \\",
              "detail": "what you would write anyway",
              "sub": "no special call at all",
              "label": "normal",
              "atWord": 18.25
            },
            {
              "text": "    .fill(\"2026-08-01\")",
              "detail": "and it fills the sealed input",
              "sub": "the date lands",
              "label": "filled",
              "atWord": 33.083
            }
          ]
